"{\n  \"reasoning\": \"INFEASIBLE: With a 500\u202f\u00b5W power budget the tail current is limited to Itail \u2264 75.8\u202f\u00b5A (since P = VDD\u00b72\u00b7Itail). Each input transistor then carries \u226437.9\u202f\u00b5A. Even at the most favorable device length (L=2\u202f\u00b5m) and the highest allowed gm/Id (24\u202fV\u207b\u00b9), the achievable transconductance is gm1 = 24\u00b737.9\u202f\u00b5A \u2248 0.91\u202fmS. The output conductances of the NMOS and PMOS loads at L=2\u202f\u00b5m (gm/gds \u2248 580 and 1258) give gds2 \u2248 1.6\u202f\u00b5S and gds4 \u2248 0.72\u202f\u00b5S, so the DC gain gm1/(gds2+gds4) \u2248 0.91\u202fmS / 2.3\u202f\u00b5S \u2248 395 (\u224852\u202fdB), well below the required 65\u202fdB. Achieving 65\u202fdB would require gm1 \u2248 1.7\u202fmS, which would need gm/Id \u2248 45\u202fV\u207b\u00b9, outside the allowed range (4\u201324\u202fV\u207b\u00b9). Therefore the specifications cannot be met with this topology and power limit.\",\n  \"gmid1\": 10,\n  \"L1_um\": 2,\n  \"gmid3\": 10,\n  \"L3_um\": 2,\n  \"gmid5\": 10,\n  \"L5_um\": 0.5,\n  \"Itail_uA\": 75\n}"